### Granot lifecycle reads and Booking/Release commands

- Case/discrepancy implementation paths remain under `/ingestion/granot/lifecycle` (`cases/[caseId]`, `discrepancies`). The old queue, Health, and forensic job URLs redirect. Booking and cancellation review for the Owner lives at `/intakes`. Choosing a waiting intake stays on `/intakes?case=` and does not jump to `/ingestion/granot/lifecycle/cases/:id`. `IntakeCasePage` fetches the case once and routes it: `kind:"booking"` gets `BookingIntakeWorkbench`; `kind:"release"` gets `CancellationIntakeWorkbench`.
- **The booking intake reads as one story, in this order**, and new work belongs in whichever act it answers: (1) *What Granot sent us* — `GranotBookingStatementCard` renders the readable customer/move/money facts produced by `granot-statement-reading.ts`, the priority sentence, then the exact Granot message and Vantage's reading of it behind two drawers; (2) *Who this booking is for* — `MatchedCustomerSection` shows the matched lead, its confidence, Form submitted vs Granot via `intake-known-contacts` (chip, cards, cycle/search strings from `intake-copy`), a collapsible full-lead snapshot, and opens `LeadCandidateBrowser` when the Owner says the customer is wrong; (3) *Finish the booking* — `BookingOwnerActions`; (4) the reference drawers from `intake-reference.tsx` (what Vantage already has, every Granot update, the job lifecycle timeline), opened by default only when commands are unavailable. Booking `/intakes` rows and the technical booking case page render the same statement folded into `GranotBookingStatementAccordion`.
- **The cancellation intake is the same first and last acts**, without a customer-matching step: (1) *What Granot sent us* — the same statement card, preferring the latest Release evidence; (2) *Finish the cancellation* — `ReleaseOwnerActions`; (3) the same reference drawers. Cancellation `/intakes` rows and the technical release case page fold the same statement into `GranotBookingStatementAccordion` with `kind="cancellation"`.
- Who a booking is for is answered by `useMatchedLead(caseId)`, not by the form. It derives `chosenLead ?? pickBestCandidate(...)` during render — never from an effect — and shares one `queryKeys.granotLifecycle.candidates(caseId, { scope: "source" })` cache entry with the search panel, so the match costs no extra request. `BookingCommandForm` takes the answer as a `matchedLead` prop and asks only for the official numbers (one Binder amount, Primary Agent, optional Secondary Agent with `No split`, deposit, merchant from the Operations Registry catalog; derived split is read-only). Confirm, update, and referral official details send `primary_agent_id`, optional `secondary_agent_id`, and `total_binder_amount` via `lib/booking/officialBookingDetails.ts` — not per-agent binder rows or Add Agent. `CaseDetail` no longer chooses between a browser and a form: its caller composes one `ownerWork` node.
- `LeadCandidateResults` rows render full lead facts via `candidate-lead-facts.tsx`, and stay read-only (no selection controls) when `onSelect` is absent. `isAllowedIntakeReturn` allows `/intakes` plus safe `/intakes?...` query strings (no `://` or `//`); the technical case page may use that back-link. `/ingestion/granot` remains HTTP Automation with no inner nest. Owner live Granot webhook SSE is the top-level `/live-events` tab (`live-webhooks.tsx`). The client keeps a sliding 30-minute window of at most 80 newest receipts (`LIVE_RECEIPT_WINDOW_MS` / `LIVE_RECEIPT_WINDOW_LIMIT` in `granotLiveReceipts.ts`); heartbeats drop expired cards. `/ingestion/granot/live` permanently redirects to `/live-events`. `/granot-lifecycle` and `/granot-lifecycle/receipts` are Owner-only Receipts search (`queryKeys.granotLifecycle.receipts`). Filters live on the URL (`GRANOT_WEBHOOK_RECEIPT_FILTER_KEYS`); Owner labels only; rows link Open Job Timeline when `job_no` is present and Open Intake when `intake_case_id` is present. Subnav Receipts vs Health are exclusive. `/granot-lifecycle/health` is Owner/Admin read-only (`queryKeys.granotLifecycle.health()`), linked from Observational overview.
- **Owner-visible strings live in `components/intakes/intake-copy.ts`, never inline in an intake component.** The reader owns a moving company: say what happened, then what to do; never print a `snake_case` identifier or name a system he does not operate; every non-working state states whether anything is being lost.
- Browser code always uses the signed `/api/proxy/api/v1/...` boundary. Standard lifecycle GETs (including `operations/health`) are Owner/Admin at the proxy; candidates, creating-observation, live receipts, the receipts list GET, and every command are Owner-only. Standard/Referral create, update, cancellation, No Action, and Connect Booking to Lead forward `Idempotency-Key`; browser secrets and actor headers are stripped before trusted headers are minted.
- Server DTOs remain semantic authority for source scope, matching, candidate eligibility, masking, timeline ordering, and operations health. Admin components render those DTOs and never open operational Mongo or recompute due work, p95, rates, or alerts.
- `queryKeys.granotLifecycle` is isolated from Employee Booking reconciliation and Granot Automation. `invalidateGranotLifecycleCommandViews` is invoked after Confirm Granot Booking, Update Existing Booking, and No Action (success and `409` refetch), and after Connect Booking to Lead success (`queryKeys.granotLifecycle.connectCandidates` plus booking list/detail). Health uses `queryKeys.granotLifecycle.health()` and is not part of that command invalidation set.
- Live Owner command UI: open standard and Referral Booking cases use `booking-owner-actions`; Referral create starts with blank official fields and never shows candidate/attach controls. Open `kind:"release"`, `mode:"release"` cases use `release-owner-actions` for Create Cancellation, full Update Existing Booking, and No Action. All surfaces require server capabilities and explicit review before submit.
- Polling (case detail 15s) may refresh evidence and timelines but must preserve component-owned confirm/update/cancellation/No Action draft state. Booking replacement initializes once from the live Booking projection (including active catalog IDs), while Cancellation starts blank; neither uses Granot evidence as official defaults. `409` refetch preserves unsent values and never auto-resubmits. Booking and Release discriminants, sequences, and timeline entries never collapse. Release command capability follows the server gate; discrepancies remain false.

## Ownership Boundaries

- **Admin owns:** login/sessions, admin audit DB, UI, route handlers, TanStack Query, frontend constants, signed proxy BFF, public employee-booking nonce.
- **Main server owns:** operational DBs, business rules, sheet sync, analytics, registry, ingestion, Granot automation, Granot lifecycle, reporting delivery, Google Drive connection, reconciliation, exports.
- Do not open `vantagemovers` / `vantagemovershistorical` from admin.
- Legacy CPL is a read-only compatibility view in Operations Registry (`?tab=legacy-cpl`). Durable source/CPL/agent/merchant edits live on the other registry tabs. `/settings` is a permanent redirect, not a parallel surface.
- Mutations must invalidate the relevant query keys (lists, details, search, audit, analytics, registry, reporting) where data can change.

## Quality Practices

- Keep secrets/Mongo/auth in `server/` or route handlers — never in client components.
- Validate proxy paths stay under `VANTAGE_API_BASE_URL`; reject absolute/`://` targets.
- CLI Admin Previews do not inherit branch-only env. When the API host is a protected Preview, set Preview-only `VANTAGE_API_PROTECTION_BYPASS` to the **server** project's automation bypass (never this project's `VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET`) and pass both values with `vercel deploy --env`. Do not set the bypass on Production Admin.
- Audit mutating + CSV/export proxy requests without masking successful backend responses.
- Prefer small focused modules in the owning feature folder.
- After substantive changes: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, and relevant tests.
